      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin in adults. A single 1,700 mg dose is also above the usual maximum per dose of about 1,000 recommended (typically 850 mg to 1,000 mg). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some options that might match what you meant:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at a different frequency.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm that. I'd also suggest checking it with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order."
      }
